  "summary": "preinstall reverse shell to hardcoded remote host on npm install",
  "details": "package.json declares a preinstall lifecycle script that spawns an interactive bash with stdio redirected to a TCP socket at 147.93.157.202:8080 and pipes the session to an HTTP POST to a canarytokens.com URL. Running `npm install @nimbusedge/auth` executes this hook automatically, opening a reverse shell that gives the remote endpoint arbitrary command execution on the installer's host before any application code runs. The callback is plaintext HTTP with no authentication, and the destination IP and canarytokens URL are hardcoded in the manifest.",
